      "id": 1,
      "text": "Nevada, Missouri was originally called \"Hog Eye\" when settlers platted it in 1855.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nevada%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "From 1897 to 1933, the town hosted the Weltmer Institute of Suggestive Therapeutics, drawing so many patients that the railroad added new trains to its schedule.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
